
You are implementing a new feature in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central to enhance user onboarding with an interactive tour on a Sales Invoice page.
You need to design an interactive guide for the Sales Invoice page that communicates the purpose of each field and action concisely.
Each correct answer presents part of the solution. Which three actions should you take?

Using detailed descriptions for each field and action can overwhelm users and detract from the clarity of the teaching tips.
Using sequential tips for invoice creation guides users step-by-step through the process, making the onboarding experience structured and informative.
Defining properties for each field, such as AboutTitle and AboutText, provides clear explanations of what each field is about and what actions can be performed.
Enabling the tour to start from the teaching tip allows users to initiate the tour at their convenience, enhancing flexibility and user control.
Using bold text extensively overwhelms users and detracts from the clarity of the teaching tips.



