A company implements a new feature in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central to enhance user experience on the Customer List page.
Create a view highlighting customers with balances greater than 500 LCY, sorted by name in ascending order, ensuring a unique layout.
Each correct answer presents part of the solution. Which three actions should be performed?

Defining a view in the page customization object allows for creating a customized view on the Customer List page, essential for meeting task requirements. Setting the SharedLayout property to false ensures the view has a unique layout, aligning with the goal of a distinct presentation. Filtering customers with a balance greater than 500 LCY is crucial for displaying the correct data set. Modifying the layout to add a new column is not feasible within a view, as views cannot introduce new columns.
Setting the Caption property is a standard practice but does not affect the functionality or appearance required by the question.

