Your organization is preparing to launch a new Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central app on Microsoft AppSource. The app will offer different levels of functionality and pricing options.

You need to ensure the app can be purchased through Microsoft AppSource.

Each correct answer presents part of the solution. Which three actions should you perform?


To prepare a Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central app for transactability on Microsoft AppSource, it is essential to enable transactability in Microsoft Partner Center,
define pricing plans, and map these plans to entitlements using the Service ID.
These steps ensure that the app can be purchased and managed through Microsoft AppSource, providing customers with the appropriate features based on their selected plan.
Implementing a custom payment gateway is not necessary as Microsoft AppSource handles payment processing.
Creating a custom entitlement mapping is not necessary for enabling transactability on Microsoft AppSource, which uses Microsoft's entitlement framework.


