You are developing a new feature in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central that involves complex calculations for sales orders. You have created several test codeunits.

You need to automate the execution of these test codeunits to ensure they run independently without affecting each other.


Setting TestIsolation to Codeunit ensures that all changes to the database are rolled back after each test codeunit executes,
maintaining independence between tests.
Using a test runner codeunit does not inherently automate the execution of test codeunits independently, as it requires additional configuration to ensure isolation and automation.
Setting TransactionModel to AutoCommit would commit changes to the database, contradicting the requirement of running tests independently.
Using the OnBeforeTestRun trigger for initialization does not ensure test isolation, as it does not address the requirement of running tests independently without affecting each other.


